## Why This Question Is Asked

This question assesses native bridging fundamentals, cross-platform API design, and UI lifecycle management. It evaluates whether the candidate can design a minimal, reliable UX primitive that behaves consistently across iOS and Android.

## Key Concepts

- React Native native module bridging
- Cross-platform UI overlays and lifecycle management
- Message queuing to handle rapid toast requests
- Testing and debugging mobile-specific rendering

## Code Example

```javascript
import { NativeModules } from 'react-native';
const { ToastModule } = NativeModules;

// Display a toast message
ToastModule.showToast('Item added to cart', 3000);

// Position toasts at the top of the screen
ToastModule.setPosition('top');

// Manually dismiss the current toast
ToastModule.hideToast();
```

```javascript
// React hook wrapper for the ToastModule
import { useEffect, useCallback } from 'react';
import { ToastModule } from './native/ToastModule';

export function useToast() {
  const show = useCallback((message, durationMs = 3000) => {
    ToastModule.showToast(message, durationMs);
  }, []);

  const hide = useCallback(() => {
    ToastModule.hideToast();
  }, []);

  const setPosition = useCallback((position) => {
    ToastModule.setPosition(position);
  }, []);

  return { show, hide, setPosition };
}
```

